## Assumptions

1. Users are identified by their role for now. Log In isn't modelled as a use case.
2. Patients can book, reschedule, and cancel their own appointments.
3. If patient requested appointments, then they are confirmed automatically. If staff requested appointments, it is booked but the patient must confirm.
4. The professional records the follow-up in Conduct Consultation, but staff books it.
5. External physicians don't use the system, but staff records their referrals for clinic's physicians.
6. HealthCare Professional records are created by an unmodeled Administration Staff Manager, outside the scope of this iteration. After that, professionals maintain their own information and schedule.
7. Professionals can view medical records only for their assigned patients, including outside a consultation.
8. Administrative Staff handles billing, and the invoice and payment are done together.
9. Clinic locations already exist in the system.
10. All healthcare professionals (physicians, specialists, nurses) can do the same things in the system.
11. External systems (RAMQ, pharmacies, provincial systems) are out of scope and not shown as actors.
12. Authorized clinic staff depends in this context. Healthcare Professional for patient's medical actions and Administrative Staff for the rest